power: supply: sc27xx_fuel_gauge: UMP9620's saved capacity is in 0.1 %, and capacity stays within 0-100

The FGU's always-on user area keeps the last capacity across a reboot, and the boot after Android reads it back.
Android keeps it there in 0.1 %: on the U30 Air the first mainline boot with a charger driver (patch 0009) read
575 and reported capacity 575. Until then the status was Full (0006's fallback), and the calibration that runs
outside charging forced anything above 100 back to 100, so nobody saw it. On UMP9620 the value is now read and
saved in 0.1 %, and the reported capacity is clamped to 0-100: while charging nothing calibrates the coulomb count.

--- a/drivers/power/supply/sc27xx_fuel_gauge.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/sc27xx_fuel_gauge.c
@@ -275,6 +275,10 @@
 	 */
 	udelay(200);
 
+	/* UMP9620: Android keeps the capacity here in 0.1 % (575 at 57.5 %); so does this driver */
+	if (data->var == &ump9620_info)
+		cap = clamp(cap, 0, 100) * 10;
+
 	ret = regmap_update_bits(data->regmap,
 				 data->base + SC27XX_FGU_USER_AREA_SET,
 				 SC27XX_FGU_CAP_AREA_MASK, cap);
@@ -309,6 +313,9 @@
 		return ret;
 
 	*cap = value & SC27XX_FGU_CAP_AREA_MASK;
+	/* UMP9620: in 0.1 % (see sc27xx_fgu_save_last_cap()) */
+	if (data->var == &ump9620_info)
+		*cap = min(DIV_ROUND_CLOSEST(*cap, 10), 100);
 	return 0;
 }
 
@@ -702,7 +709,8 @@
 		if (ret)
 			goto error;
 
-		val->intval = value;
+		/* the coulomb count can run past either end while charging, when nothing calibrates it */
+		val->intval = clamp(value, 0, 100);
 		break;
 
 	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_VOLTAGE_AVG:
